{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "h2GrwgWm6D", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-23", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 905505, "segment_id": "7L1Qf0WLOJ", "segment_broadcast_id": "h2GrwgWm6D", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Charles Gibson (New York)", "segment_description": null, "segment_duration": 60, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 905505, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "h2GrwgWm6D", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-23", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 905505, "segment_id": "ao2db8ySZP", "segment_broadcast_id": "h2GrwgWm6D", "segment_title": "Economy: Government Bailout / Senate", "segment_description": "(Studio: Charles Gibson)  Report introduced.  \n\n(Studio: Betsy Stark)  The battle in Congress over the government's 700-billion dollar bailout plan for Wall Street featured; scenes shown of the senators with Treasury Secretary Henry Paulson and Federal Reserve Board chairman Ben Bernanke.  [Senators Robert MENDENEZ, Jon TESTER, Mel MARTINEZ, Richard SHELBY\u00a0- raise questions.]  [PAULSON\u00a0- says he shares the outrage and there is blame to go around; states he welcomes oversight.]  [In response to question from Senator Christopher Dodd, BERNANKE\u00a0- outlines what would happen without a bailout.]  [Senator Jim BUNNING\u00a0- says he is frightful about the plan's lack of a solution.]  Stock Market Report.  \n\n(Studio: Charles Gibson)  Statement from President Bush at the U.N. about world concern about the turmoil in the US economy noted.  \n\n(Washington: Jake Tapper)  The view of the economic crisis from presidential candidates Senators John McCain and Barack Obama featured; details given about the importance of McCain's support for Republican backing of the proposed bill.  [McCAIN\u00a0- speaks about the Wall Street tycoons; states this issue should not be related to his vote.]  [OBAMA\u00a0- talks about the approach of the bailout plan.]  [Senator Harry REID\u00a0- says we need Republican votes.]  \n\n(Studio: Charles Gibson; Washington: George Stephanopoulos)  How this bailout rests on McCain's shoulders, how he has not made up his mind, the consensus on Capitol Hill about the need for oversight of the package with restraint on executive compensation and foreclosure relief and the likelihood of Congressional passage of a bill discussed.  \n\n(Studio: Charles Gibson)  Report introduced.  \n\n(New York: Dan Harris)  \"What if\" the bailout does not happen examined; details given of concerns about banks freezing lending as exemplifed by action by Bank of America re: a loan to McDonald's and the view of the head of Chrysler on car loans.  [\"New York Times\" editor Andrew Ross SORKIN\u2020- says if the government did nothing Main Street would really get hit; asks whether a deep recession is acceptable.]  [Wachovia analyst Jay BRYSON\u2020- says innocents would get hurt.]  [Tavakoli Structured Finance president Janet TAVAKOLI\u2020- speaks about helping struggling homeowners.] ", "segment_duration": 590, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63060.0", "legacy_segment_id": 905506, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "h2GrwgWm6D", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-23", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distri